{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.carroll.edu/faculty-staff-positions#tenure-track-position-in-civil-engineering": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Position in Civil Engineering",
      "description": "Tenure Track Position in Civil Engineering. Description: Carroll College invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position in the Department of Engineering to begin in August 2027. Applicants must have a strong commitment to teaching at the undergraduate level in a small college environment and must be qualified to teach all levels of undergraduate civil engineering courses, preferably in the subfields of geotechnical, water resources, or transportation engineering. The Civil Engineering Program is ABET accredited and has active Engineers Without Borders and ASCE student chapters. Qualifications: The successful candidate will have a Master’s degree in engineering or closely related field and the ability to obtain a Professional Engineering license within four years of hire. A Doctoral degree in engineering, a current Professional Engineering license and/or extensive professional experience is preferred. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. To Apply: For consideration, please submit the following materials electronically to employment@carroll.edu . Priority deadline is December 18, 2026; applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Completed Carroll College Application Salary and rank are commensurate with experience, education and qualifications. Carroll College is proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to creating a welcoming work environment for all. Finalists for the position will be asked to provide a written response to Carroll College’s Mission Statement . Benefits Include: Employer sponsored Medical insurance, Wellness program and Employee Assistance Program Tuition Remission for employee, and if eligible, for spouse and dependent child(ren) Potential Tuition Exchange benefits for dependent child(ren) 403(b) Retirement Plan with matching contributions from the College Employer provided Life and Long-Term disability benefits Voluntary Dental, Vision, Pet Insurance and more Other unique benefits such as tickets to home athletic events, rental of outdoor equipment, access to the campus workout facility, and more About Us: Carroll College is a leading private, liberal arts college in the American West. Carroll’s campus rests on 63 acres at the edge of downtown and historic Helena, the capital city of Montana. The surrounding beauty of the Rocky Mountains and Montana fosters wonder and awe, giving the perfect backdrop to a worldly education. More than 75 miles of hiking and biking trails are just minutes from campus, and Helena is in close proximity to the Continental Divide Trail, natural hot springs, Great Divide Ski Area and the Missouri River. Yellowstone National Park and Glacier National Park are just a few hours away. Founded in 1909, Carroll College warmly embraces its identity as a diocesan, Catholic college. Carroll represents a beacon of light in the community, welcoming all persons in a cooperative journey toward knowledge and virtue."
    },
    "https://www.carroll.edu/faculty-staff-positions#tenure-track-position-in-nursing": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Position in Nursing",
      "description": "Tenure Track Position in Nursing. Description: Carroll College invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Nursing in its CCNE-accredited Baccalaureate Nursing program, beginning in August 2027. The Nursing Department seeks an engaged educator and colleague who demonstrates excellence in teaching, strong written and verbal communication skills, a commitment to student success, and support for the Catholic and diocesan mission of Carroll College. The successful candidate will contribute to the continued excellence of our long-standing traditional and accelerated nursing pathways through classroom, laboratory, and/or clinical instruction. Primary responsibilities include teaching undergraduate nursing courses; academic advising and mentoring students; developing curriculum; assessing and evaluating student learning outcomes; and actively participating in departmental, college, and professional service. Candidates should be passionate about preparing future nursing professionals and fostering a supportive, student-centered learning environment. Qualifications: The successful candidate must have a master’s degree in nursing, at least five years of recent nursing practice, and an unencumbered Montana Registered Nurse license. We are seeking a colleague with broad nursing expertise, especially in Obstetrics and/or Pediatrics Nursing, for both our traditional and accelerated tracks. Previous teaching and simulation experience is desired but not required. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. To Apply: For consideration, please submit the following materials electronically to employment@carroll.edu . Applications will be reviewed as submitted, and the position will remain open until filled. Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Completed Carroll College Application Salary and rank are commensurate with experience, education and qualifications. Carroll College is proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to creating a welcoming work environment for all. Finalists for the position will be asked to provide a written response to Carroll College’s Mission Statement . Benefits Include: Employer-sponsored medical insurance, Wellness Program, and Employee Assistance Program Voluntary Dental, Vision, Pet Insurance and more 403(b) Retirement Plan with matching contributions from the College Employer-provided life and long-term disability benefits Tuition remission for employee, and if eligible, for spouse and dependent child(ren) Potential Tuition Exchange benefits for dependent child(ren) Other unique benefits such as tickets to home athletic events, rental of outdoor equipment, access to the campus workout facility, and more About Us: Carroll College is a leading private, liberal arts college in the American West. Carroll’s campus rests on 63 acres at the edge of downtown and historic Helena, the capital city of Montana. The surrounding beauty of the Rocky Mountains and Montana fosters wonder and awe, giving the perfect backdrop to a worldly education. More than 75 miles of hiking and biking trails are just minutes from campus, and Helena is in close proximity to the Continental Divide Trail, natural hot springs, Great Divide Ski Area and the Missouri River. Yellowstone National Park and Glacier National Park are just a few hours away. Founded in 1909, Carroll College warmly embraces its identity as a diocesan, Catholic college. Carroll represents a beacon of light in the community, welcoming all persons in a cooperative journey toward knowledge and virtue."
    },
    "https://www.carroll.edu/faculty-staff-positions#founding-director-master-of-educational-leadership-program": {
      "title": "Founding Director, Master of Educational Leadership Program",
      "description": "Founding Director, Master of Educational Leadership Program. Description: Carroll College invites applications for a full-time, 12-month, non-tenure-track faculty position to serve as the Founding Director of the Master of Educational Leadership Program. This is an exciting leadership opportunity to develop, launch, and lead a fully online, asynchronous graduate program designed to prepare experienced educators and professionals for leadership roles in schools, districts, educational organizations, and policy settings. Reporting to the Senior Vice President for Academic Affairs, the Director will collaborate across campus and with external partners to design curriculum, oversee online course delivery, recruit and support faculty, advance student success, coordinate assessment efforts, and ensure the program remains responsive to the needs of schools, districts, and education professionals. The successful candidate is expected to maintain a consistent physical presence on campus to fulfill teaching, service, and institutional responsibilities. As the inaugural leader of the program, the successful candidate will play a critical role in creating a mission-aligned graduate offering that prepares ethical, effective, and service-oriented educational leaders. The position requires creativity, initiative, organization, and a collaborative leadership style to establish the program's academic foundation and support its long-term growth and success. The goal is to enroll the program's first cohort in Fall 2027. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: The Founding Director will lead the development of the Master of Educational Leadership curriculum, program policies, and supporting materials for review and approval through the College's shared governance processes. The Director will design a curriculum that serves both aspiring and current educational leaders while creating opportunities for future specialization and program expansion. Working closely with instructional designers and academic partners, the Director will ensure the development and delivery of high-quality online, asynchronous courses that reflect best practices in graduate education. The Director will also ensure curriculum alignment with relevant leadership standards, state requirements, workforce needs, and Carroll College's mission. The Director will recruit, supervise, mentor, and support adjunct faculty with expertise in educational leadership, administration, policy, curriculum, assessment, and related fields. Teaching graduate-level courses within the program will be expected as appropriate. In partnership with Enrollment Management, Marketing, and Academic Affairs, the Director will support student recruitment, admissions, retention, and student success initiatives. The Director will cultivate and maintain partnerships with schools, districts, educational organizations, and community stakeholders to strengthen the program's visibility, relevance, and impact. Additional responsibilities include coordinating program assessment activities, preparing accreditation-related reports when applicable, overseeing continuous improvement initiatives, advising and mentoring students, managing program budgets and resources, and representing the program both internally and externally. The Director will also perform other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications: The successful candidate will have a graduate degree in Education, Educational Leadership, School Administration, Curriculum and Instruction, or a closely related field. Applicants should demonstrate professional experience in K–12 education, higher education, educational leadership, school administration, or a related area of practice. Experience with curriculum development and program-level assessment of student learning outcomes is required, as is experience with online teaching and learning. Preferred Qualifications: A terminal degree in Education, Educational Leadership, School Administration, Curriculum and Instruction, or a closely related field is preferred. Additional preferred qualifications include experience serving as a school principal, district administrator, instructional leader, or higher education program leader. Candidates with knowledge of Montana educator preparation requirements, licensure pathways, and school leadership standards are particularly encouraged to apply. Experience developing, launching, or leading graduate academic programs, as well as experience recruiting, mentoring, and supervising adjunct faculty, is highly desirable. The ideal candidate will also demonstrate familiarity with online graduate education and the needs of adult learners and have experience designing and delivering instruction using Moodle or a comparable learning management system. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. To Apply: For primary consideration, please submit the following materials electronically to employment@carroll.edu by August 15, 2026. Applications will be reviewed as submitted and the position will remain open until filled. Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae Completed Carroll College Application Salary is commensurate with experience, education and qualifications. Carroll College is proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to creating a welcoming work environment for all. If you have questions about the position, please contact the chair of the search committee, Dr. Jeremy Johnson at jjohnson@carroll.edu . F inalists for the position will be asked to provide a written response to Carroll College’s Mission Statement . Benefits Include: Employer sponsored Medical insurance, Wellness program and Employee Assistance Program Voluntary Dental, Vision, Pet Insurance and more 403(b) Retirement Plan with matching contributions from the College Potential Tuition Remission benefit for employee, spouse and dependent children and potential Tuition Exchange benefit for dependent children Employer provided Life and Long-Term disability benefits Other unique benefits such as tickets to home athletic events, rental of outdoor equipment, access to the campus workout facility, and more About Us: Carroll College is a leading private, liberal arts college in the American West. Carroll’s campus rests on 63 acres at the edge of downtown and historic Helena, the capital city of Montana. The surrounding beauty of the Rocky Mountains and Montana fosters wonder and awe, giving the perfect backdrop to a worldly education. More than 75 miles of hiking and biking trails are just minutes from campus, and Helena is in close proximity to the Continental Divide Trail, natural hot springs, Great Divide Ski Area and the Missouri River. Yellowstone National Park and Glacier National Park are just a few hours away. Founded in 1909, Carroll College warmly embraces its identity as a diocesan, Catholic college. Carroll represents a beacon of light in the community, welcoming members of all religious faiths and all persons of good will in a cooperative journey toward knowledge and virtue."
    },
    "https://www.carroll.edu/faculty-staff-positions#part-time-clinical-nursing-faculty": {
      "title": "Part-time Clinical Nursing Faculty",
      "description": "Part-time Clinical Nursing Faculty. Description: Carroll College invites applications for a part-time, non-tenure track, Clinical Nursing Faculty to join our Nursing Baccalaureate program. This position would provide supervision, demonstration, and collaborative evaluation of student performance in a clinical or laboratory setting . The Department of Nursing is seeking a colleague who possesses exceptional communication skills (both written and verbal), is committed to academic and clinical excellence, is enthusiastic about student interactions, and who supports the mission of the college. Qualifications: The successful candidate must have a Bachelor’s Degree in Nursing as well as an unencumbered Montana Registered Nurse license. National certification in your clinical area is required within 1 year of employment. Continuing educatoin in your clinical area is required and National certification in your clinical areaq is encouraged within one year of employment. We are seeking a colleague with broad clinical experience in adult and pediatric nursing. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. To Apply: For consideration, please submit the following materials electronically to employment@carroll.edu . Applications will be reviewed as submitted and the position will remain open until filled. Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae Completed Carroll College Application Salary is commensurate with experience, education and qualifications. Carroll College is proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to creating a welcoming work environment for all. Finalists for the position will be asked to provide a written response to Carroll College’s Mission Statement . Benefits Include: Employer sponsored Medical insurance, Wellness program and Employee Assistance Program Voluntary Dental, Vision, Pet Insurance and more 403(b) Retirement Plan with matching contributions from the College Employer provided Life and Long-Term disability benefits Tuition Remission for employee, and if eligible, for spouse and dependent child(ren) Potential Tuition Exchange benefits for dependent child(ren) Other unique benefits such as tickets to home athletic events, rental of outdoor equipment, access to the campus workout facility, and more About Us: Carroll College is a leading private, liberal arts college in the American West. Carroll’s campus rests on 63 acres at the edge of downtown and historic Helena, the capital city of Montana. The surrounding beauty of the Rocky Mountains and Montana fosters wonder and awe, giving the perfect backdrop to a worldly education. More than 75 miles of hiking and biking trails are just minutes from campus, and Helena is in close proximity to the Continental Divide Trail, natural hot springs, Great Divide Ski Area and the Missouri River. Yellowstone National Park and Glacier National Park are just a few hours away. Founded in 1909, Carroll College warmly embraces its identity as a diocesan, Catholic college. Carroll represents a beacon of light in the community, welcoming members of all religious faiths and all persons of good will in a cooperative journey toward knowledge and virtue."
    },
    "https://www.carroll.edu/faculty-staff-positions#principal-faculty-for-physician-assistant-program": {
      "title": "Principal Faculty for Physician Assistant Program",
      "description": "Principal Faculty for Physician Assistant Program. Carroll College invites applications for the position of Principal Faculty in the developing Physician Assistant Program. This is an exciting opportunity to play a pivotal role in developing a new physician assistant program. The Principal Faculty position is a full-time 12-month faculty appointment in the Physician Assistant Studies program with a rank commensurate with qualifications and experience. This position reports directly to the Physician Assistant Program Director. Under the supervision of the Program Director, the faculty member will support the development and implementation of the program curriculum and competencies to meet current practice standards as they relate to the PA role. Responsibilities will support the didactic and clinical phases of the program. Once students are enrolled in the program, a significant amount of time will be devoted to teaching in the didactic phase of the program. This position requires excellent interpersonal, organizational and time management skills. The ideal candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to student success and support, have excellent critical thinking, conflict resolution, and decision-making skills. Qualifications Required Advanced degree in a health-related field. For Physician Assistants/Physician Associates: M aster’s degree (or higher) from an accredited Physician Assistant/Physician Associate program. Currently licensed physician assistant in good standing in the state of Montana or eligible to obtain licensure in Montana. Current NCCPA certification. Minimum of 5 years of clinical experience as a PA. For non-PAs: Must hold a MD, DO, or PhD. Minimum of 5 years of experience in related field. Proficiency in basic computer technology and the ability to learn new course learning management system(s), learning platforms and educational technologies. Must have the ability to occasionally travel to clinical sites within the state and region to conduct on-site student assessments. Preferred Prior faculty experience at an accredited physician assistant program. Prior experience teaching or precepting physician assistant and/or medical students. Previous experience teaching in the basic sciences Previous administrative experience. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. To Apply For consideration, please submit the following materials electronically to employment@carroll.edu . Applications will be reviewed as submitted and the position will remain open until filled. The ideal candidate would be available to start no later than July 1, 2026. Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae Completed Carroll College Application Salary is commensurate with experience, education and qualifications. Carroll College is proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to creating a welcoming work environment for all. Finalists for the position will be asked to provide a written response to Carroll College’s Mission Statement . Benefits Employer sponsored Medical insurance, Wellness program and Employee Assistance Program Voluntary Dental, Vision, Pet Insurance and more 403(b) Retirement Plan with matching contributions from the College Employer provided Life and Long-Term disability benefits Tuition Remission for employee, and if eligible, for spouse and dependent child(ren) Potential Tuition Exchange benefits for dependent child(ren) Other unique benefits such as tickets to home athletic events, rental of outdoor equipment, access to the campus workout facility, and more About Us Carroll College is a leading private, liberal arts college in the American West. Carroll’s campus rests on 63 acres at the edge of downtown and historic Helena, the capital city of Montana. The surrounding beauty of the Rocky Mountains and Montana fosters wonder and awe, giving the perfect backdrop to a worldly education. More than 75 miles of hiking and biking trails are just minutes from campus, and Helena is in close proximity to the Continental Divide Trail, natural hot springs, Great Divide Ski Area and the Missouri River. Yellowstone National Park and Glacier National Park are just a few hours away. Founded in 1909, Carroll College warmly embraces its identity as a diocesan, Catholic college. Carroll represents a beacon of light in the community, welcoming all persons in a cooperative journey toward knowledge and virtue."
    },
    "https://www.carroll.edu/faculty-staff-positions#area-coordinator": {
      "title": "Area Coordinator",
      "description": "Area Coordinator. Description: Carroll College seeks interested candidates for a live-on Area Coordinator position to help us live out our motto, “Not for School, but for Life.” With the mountains at our doorstep, we embrace the adventure of the college experience, including the opportunities and challenges that shape students for life at college and beyond. We are looking for a team member who will continue our commitment to an excellent student experience. The Residential Life and Housing Department plays a vital role in advancing the mission of Carroll College. We seek a collaborative partner who is deeply invested in students and their holistic wellness, community development, attentive to innovative processes, and eager to contribute to our program's growth. In coordination with the other Residential Life & Housing professional staff, this position is responsible for promoting a safe and vibrant living and learning environment for approximately 400 students of our 900+ residential student population. In their role, Area Coordinators provide supervision of: 6 to 12 Resident Assistants Management and operation of community residence hall(s) to support healthy and safe living and learning environments. Support for key housing operations and committee engagement. Time management, email management, priority setting, and general administrative skills to contribute to departmental processes and success. Promotion of holistic and educational opportunities in student community life, through the lens of a Catholic Liberal Arts College. Our foundations include a focus on the development of the whole person, student development theory, learning outcomes, and organizational theory. Promotion of an intentional interaction model. Utilization of a student-centered and restorative approach as a conduct administrator. Customer service perspective and skills. Utilize collaboration, teamwork, support, and compassionate candor as core aspects of their professional toolset. 37.5 hours per week, inclusive of office hours, staff meetings and programming, and community engagement. Regular use of the Google Suite for communication, data management, and process management. Utilize the eRezLife Housing Software to manage all residential operations of their community. Assignment to a functional area of Residential Life and Housing, including Housing and Assignments, Training and Development, Co-Curricular Learning Model Development, Summer Conferencing, and Student Conduct. This position serves as part of a year-round weekly on-call rotation. This position has a weekly commitment to an evening staff meeting, and some additional weekend and evening commitments. Qualifications: The successful candidate will have a bachelor’s degree in education, educational psychology, counseling, or a related field. They will also have at least one year of experience in Residential Life and/or Housing as a student or professional staff member, or experience in a related area. The successful candidate will be dedicated to student success, understand and appreciate a liberal arts education, possess excellent communication and organizational skills, exhibit professionalism, and demonstrate the ability to successfully collaborate with and engage faculty, staff, administrators, and students. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis without the need for employer sponsorship now or in the future. For this position, Carroll College will not sponsor or take over sponsorship of employment visas classifications. To Apply: For consideration, please submit the following materials electronically to employment@carroll.edu . Applications will be reviewed as submitted and the position will remain open until filled. Cover letter Resume Completed Carroll College Application Salary is commensurate with experience, education and qualifications. Carroll College is proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to creating a welcoming work environment for all. Finalists for the position will be asked to provide a written response to Carroll College’s Mission Statement . Benefits Include: Employer sponsored Medical insurance, Wellness program and Employee Assistance Program Voluntary Dental, Vision, Pet Insurance and more 403(b) Retirement Plan with matching contributions from the College Employer provided Life and Long-Term disability benefits Tuition Remission for employee, and if eligible, for spouse and dependent child(ren) Potential Tuition Exchange benefits for dependent child(ren) Very generous Holiday, Vacation, Sick and other Leave benefits to include up to 20 days of paid holidays Other unique benefits such as tickets to home athletic events, rental of outdoor equipment, access to the campus workout facility, and more About Us: Carroll College is a leading private, liberal arts college in the American West. Carroll’s campus rests on 63 acres at the edge of downtown and historic Helena, the capital city of Montana. The surrounding beauty of the Rocky Mountains and Montana fosters wonder and awe, giving the perfect backdrop to a worldly education. More than 75 miles of hiking and biking trails are just minutes from campus, and Helena is in close proximity to the Continental Divide Trail, natural hot springs, Great Divide Ski Area and the Missouri River. Yellowstone National Park and Glacier National Park are just a few hours away. Founded in 1909, Carroll College warmly embraces its identity as a diocesan, Catholic college. Carroll represents a beacon of light in the community, welcoming all persons in a cooperative journey toward knowledge and virtue."
    },
    "https://www.carroll.edu/faculty-staff-positions#collections-librarian": {
      "title": "Collections Librarian",
      "description": "Collections Librarian. Description: Carroll College Carroll College invites applications for the position of Collections Librarian. This role is responsible for the strategic development, management, and accessibility of the Library’s collections in support of the College’s academic mission. The Collections Librarian evaluates, acquires, catalogs, and manages a wide range of resources, including print books, eBooks, DVDs, electronic resources, serials, and other library materials. The successful candidate will lead collection development efforts, assess and maintain electronic information resources, and oversee the acquisition and management of print serials. This position serves as a key liaison to academic departments, the TRAILS consortium, and other library-related organizations, fostering collaboration to ensure collections effectively support teaching, learning, and research needs. In addition, the Collections Librarian provides reference and instructional support through individual consultations, classroom instruction, telephone assistance, and electronic communication. The position also contributes to the development of online instructional materials, research guides, and other web-based resources that enhance access to library services and collections. This is an 11.5 month appointment working 37.5 hours per week. Qualifications: The successful candidate will have Masters of Library Science from an ALA-accredited graduate program plus one year of electronic resources work experience in an academic library or similar setting as well as knowledge of, or experience with, library-specific information systems and technologies, such as integrated library systems, content management systems, and institutional repositories. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis without the need for employer sponsorship now or in the future. For this position, Carroll College will not sponsor or take over sponsorship of employment visas classifications. To Apply: For priority consideration, please submit the following materials electronically to employment@carroll.edu by November 9, 2026. Applications will be reviewed as submitted and the position will remain open until filled. Cover letter Resume Completed Carroll College Application Salary is commensurate with experience, education and qualifications. Carroll College is proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to creating a welcoming work environment for all. Finalists for the position will be asked to provide a written response to Carroll College’s Mission Statement . Benefits Include: Employer sponsored Medical insurance, Wellness program and Employee Assistance Program Voluntary Dental, Vision, Pet Insurance and more 403(b) Retirement Plan with matching contributions from the College Employer provided Life and Long-Term disability benefits Tuition Remission for employee, and if eligible, for spouse and dependent child(ren) Potential Tuition Exchange benefits for dependent child(ren) Very generous Holiday, Vacation, Sick and other Leave benefits to include up to 20 days of paid holidays Other unique benefits such as tickets to home athletic events, rental of outdoor equipment, access to the campus workout facility, and more About Us: Carroll College is a leading private, liberal arts college in the American West. Carroll’s campus rests on 63 acres at the edge of downtown and historic Helena, the capital city of Montana. The surrounding beauty of the Rocky Mountains and Montana fosters wonder and awe, giving the perfect backdrop to a worldly education. More than 75 miles of hiking and biking trails are just minutes from campus, and Helena is in close proximity to the Continental Divide Trail, natural hot springs, Great Divide Ski Area and the Missouri River. Yellowstone National Park and Glacier National Park are just a few hours away. Founded in 1909, Carroll College warmly embraces its identity as a diocesan, Catholic college. Carroll represents a beacon of light in the community, welcoming all persons in a cooperative journey toward knowledge and virtue."
    },
    "https://www.carroll.edu/faculty-staff-positions#director-of-career-services": {
      "title": "Director of Career Services",
      "description": "Director of Career Services. Description: Carroll College invites applicants for a Director of Career Services. This position is responsible for leading Carroll College’s career development and internship programs, helping students prepare for successful entry into the workforce, graduate school, and professional careers. This position manages career-related events, employer partnerships, internship opportunities, career readiness programming, and experiential learning initiatives. Working collaboratively with academic departments, faculty, employers, and campus partners, the Director develops and expands internship, job shadowing, and employment opportunities while integrating career preparedness into the student experience. Responsibilities include overseeing the academic internship registration and approval process, managing employer relations and affiliation agreements, administering career services technology platforms, maintaining career-related website content, and providing career guidance and professional development resources to students. The position also supports additional departmental and institutional initiatives as assigned. Qualifications: The successful candidate will have a Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Education, Counseling or related field, plus 3 years’ experience related to education and career counseling. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis without the need for employer sponsorship now or in the future. For this position, Carroll College will not sponsor or take over sponsorship of employment visas classifications. To Apply: For priority consideration, please submit the following materials electronically to employment@carroll.edu . Applications will be reviewed as submitted and the position will remain open until filled. Cover letter Resume Completed Carroll College Application Salary is commensurate with experience, education and qualifications. Carroll College is proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to creating a welcoming work environment for all. Finalists for the position will be asked to provide a written response to Carroll College’s Mission Statement . Benefits Include: Employer sponsored Medical insurance, Wellness program and Employee Assistance Program Voluntary Dental, Vision, Pet Insurance and more 403(b) Retirement Plan with matching contributions from the College Employer provided Life and Long-Term disability benefits Tuition Remission for employee, and if eligible, for spouse and dependent child(ren) Potential Tuition Exchange benefits for dependent child(ren) Very generous Holiday, Vacation, Sick and other Leave benefits to include up to 20 days of paid holidays Other unique benefits such as tickets to home athletic events, rental of outdoor equipment, access to the campus workout facility, and more About Us: Carroll College is a leading private, liberal arts college in the American West. Carroll’s campus rests on 63 acres at the edge of downtown and historic Helena, the capital city of Montana. The surrounding beauty of the Rocky Mountains and Montana fosters wonder and awe, giving the perfect backdrop to a worldly education. More than 75 miles of hiking and biking trails are just minutes from campus, and Helena is in close proximity to the Continental Divide Trail, natural hot springs, Great Divide Ski Area and the Missouri River. Yellowstone National Park and Glacier National Park are just a few hours away. Founded in 1909, Carroll College warmly embraces its identity as a diocesan, Catholic college. Carroll represents a beacon of light in the community, welcoming all persons in a cooperative journey toward knowledge and virtue."
    },
    "https://www.carroll.edu/faculty-staff-positions#custodian": {
      "title": "Custodian",
      "description": "Custodian. Description: Carroll College is seeking a full-time Custodian. The successful applicant must be self-motivated, ambitious, reliable, and detail oriented. This person will perform cleaning tasks on campus. This position is also considered a general maintenance worker and is required to assist in performing preventive maintenance on non-electrical equipment and building infrastructures and assist in snow removal, moving of miscellaneous items on campus and assists other craftsmen in all phases of maintenance. A $500 Retention Bonus will be given after the employee successfully completes 6 months of employment in the Facilities department. A second $500 Retention Bonus will be given after the employee successfully completes one full year of employment in the Facilities department. Qualifications: The successful candidate must have High School diploma or equivalent GED and some experience in custodial work. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis without the need for employer sponsorship now or in the future. For this position, Carroll College will not sponsor or take over sponsorship of employment visas classifications. To Apply: For consideration, please either: Complete the Carroll College Application for Employment and email it to employment@carroll.edu or mail it to Carroll College HR – 1601 North Benton Avenue – Helena, MT 59625. Stop by the Human Resources Office located in O’Connell Hall – Room 213 to pick up an application. Submit a Cover Letter, Resume and the Carroll College Application for Employment electronically to employment@carroll.edu or mail it to Carroll College HR – 1601 North Benton Avenue – Helena, MT 59625. Position will remain open until filled. Salary is commensurate with experience, education and qualifications. Carroll College is proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to creating an inclusive working environment for all. Benefits Include: Employer sponsored Medical insurance, Wellness program and Employee Assistance Program Voluntary Dental, Vision, Pet Insurance and more 403(b) Retirement Plan with matching contributions from the College Employer provided Life and Long-Term disability benefits Tuition Remission for employee, and if eligible, for spouse and dependent child(ren) Potential Tuition Exchange benefits for dependent child(ren) Very generous Holiday, Vacation, Sick and other Leave benefits to include up to 20 days of paid holidays Other unique benefits such as tickets to home athletic events, rental of outdoor equipment, access to the campus workout facility, and more About Us: Carroll College is a leading private, liberal arts college in the American West. Carroll’s campus rests on 63 acres at the edge of downtown and historic Helena, the capital city of Montana. The surrounding beauty of the Rocky Mountains and Montana fosters wonder and awe, giving the perfect backdrop to a worldly education. More than 75 miles of hiking and biking trails are just minutes from campus, and Helena is in close proximity to the Continental Divide Trail, natural hot springs, Great Divide Ski Area and the Missouri River. Yellowstone National Park and Glacier National Park are just a few hours away. Founded in 1909, Carroll College warmly embraces its identity as a diocesan, Catholic college. Carroll represents a beacon of light in the community, welcoming all persons in a cooperative journey toward knowledge and virtue."
    },
    "https://www.carroll.edu/faculty-staff-positions#head-dance-coach-part-time": {
      "title": "Head Dance Coach - Part-time",
      "description": "Head Dance Coach - Part-time. Description: Carroll College is seeking applicants for a part-time Head Dance Coach. Responsibilities for this position include oversight of all aspects of the day-to-day operations, including but not limited to: scheduling of dance competitions; coordination of performance-based events; the recruitment and retention of quality student-athletes; fiscal management of the operating budget; skill and technique development; donor fundraising; alumni and community relations; and possible additional duties within the Department of Athletics. The successful candidate must be able to develop positive relationships with faculty, staff, students, media, alumni, and donors while interacting successfully with department personnel and the college community. The Head Dance Coach must manage the dance program in compliance with all national association, conference and institutional rules and regulations, while aligning the management of the dance program with the mission of Carroll College. Qualifications: The successful candidate will have dance instruction experience. Preferably, experience directing a dance program in a collegiate or secondary educational setting, along with demonstrated leadership, developed interpersonal communication skills and the ability to support the mission of the college. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis without the need for employer sponsorship now or in the future. For this position, Carroll College will not sponsor or take over sponsorship of employment visas classifications. To Apply: For consideration, please submit the following materials electronically to employment@carroll.edu . Applications will be reviewed as submitted and the position will remain open until filled. Cover letter Resume Completed Carroll College Application Salary is commensurate with experience, education and qualifications. Carroll College is proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to creating a welcoming work environment for all. About Us: Carroll College is a leading private, liberal arts college in the American West. Carroll’s campus rests on 63 acres at the edge of downtown and historic Helena, the capital city of Montana. The surrounding beauty of the Rocky Mountains and Montana fosters wonder and awe, giving the perfect backdrop to a worldly education. More than 75 miles of hiking and biking trails are just minutes from campus, and Helena is in close proximity to the Continental Divide Trail, natural hot springs, Great Divide Ski Area and the Missouri River. Yellowstone National Park and Glacier National Park are just a few hours away. Founded in 1909, Carroll College warmly embraces its identity as a diocesan, Catholic college. Carroll represents a beacon of light in the community, welcoming all persons in a cooperative journey toward knowledge and virtue."
    },
    "https://www.carroll.edu/faculty-staff-positions#special-event-team-members-part-time": {
      "title": "Special Event Team Members- Part-time",
      "description": "Special Event Team Members- Part-time. Carroll College is seeking dependable, service-oriented individuals to join our Special Events Team (SET). This position supports Carroll College's commitment to providing a safe, secure, and welcoming environment during athletic contests, campus events, and other large gatherings. Under the direction of the Director of Campus Security and Public Safety, SET members provide event safety and security support, emergency response assistance, crowd management, traffic and parking coordination, and guest services. Team members help ensure compliance with applicable safety regulations, fire codes, College policies, and emergency preparedness procedures while promoting a positive experience for students, employees, visitors, and community members attending College events. This is a part-time, as-needed position requiring strong customer service skills, professionalism, reliability, and sound judgment. The successful candidate must be able to work flexible hours, including evenings, weekends, and special events as assigned. Previous experience in security, public safety, event operations, or customer service is preferred but not required. This position offers an excellent opportunity to contribute to the safety, success, and positive experience of Carroll College events while serving the campus and surrounding community. Qualifications: Qualified candidates must be at least 18 years of age and possess strong communication, customer service, and situational awareness skills. Candidates should be able to work effectively in a team environment, maintain professionalism in dynamic event settings, and demonstrate the physical ability to stand and walk for extended periods and lift or carry basic equipment. An interest in public safety, event operations, security, or emergency response is preferred. Qualified candidates must complete all required training and adher e to College policies and safety procedures. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis without the need for employer sponsorship now or in the future. For this position, Carroll College will not sponsor or take over sponsorship of employment visas classifications. To Apply: For consideration, please submit the Carroll College Application electronically to employment@carroll.edu . Applications will be reviewed as submitted. Pay will vary by event. Carroll College is proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to creating a welcoming work environment for all. About Us: Carroll College is a leading private, liberal arts college in the American West. Carroll’s campus rests on 63 acres at the edge of downtown and historic Helena, the capital city of Montana. The surrounding beauty of the Rocky Mountains and Montana fosters wonder and awe, giving the perfect backdrop to a worldly education. More than 75 miles of hiking and biking trails are just minutes from campus, and Helena is in close proximity to the Continental Divide Trail, natural hot springs, Great Divide Ski Area and the Missouri River. Yellowstone National Park and Glacier National Park are just a few hours away. Founded in 1909, Carroll College warmly embraces its identity as a diocesan, Catholic college. Carroll represents a beacon of light in the community, welcoming all persons in a cooperative journey toward knowledge and virtue."
    }
  },
